= Staal and the Banners

Weeks ago, Staal reached out to the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> youth organizations and the Banners to gauge their interest in participating in the Commonwealth Institute to Promote Youth Fitness. The program, led by retired Commonwealth Army officers, aims to teach "military sports" to young workers.

We've taken a non-committal stance, putting off the issue until after the elections, and now, the General himself is chancellor. 

We can either build goodwill and strengthen the Banners through our participation, or maintain our total opposition against the presidential cabinets and boycott it.

- @yay
- @nay

@yay
title: Approve the participation of the Banners and our youth organizations in the *Youth Corps*.
unavailable-subtitle: The party is too distrustful of Staal to allow this.
choose-if: staal_marcher_support >= 4 or knight_strength >= center_strength
on-arrival: staal_marcher_support += 2; staal_marcher_r += 1; banner_militancy += 0.04; banner_strength += 125; commons_marcher -= 4; disfavored_marcher -= 4; nationalism += 10

The Banners is now officially participating in the Commonwealth Institute to Promote Youth Fitness. Their board of trustees, with our input, has swiftly established infantry and naval training schools across the country. the Banners youth are the primary recipients of specialized instruction from former and decommissioned Commonwealth Army officers, and we have secured considerable influence within the institute’s leadership.

This program has strengthened the Banners and improved our relations with Staal. However, our collaboration with an initiative authorized by the deeply unpopular [+ chancellor +] government has cost us support—many have defected to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@nay
title: We need the sharpest opposition to the new Staal cabinet. Order the Greater Worker's Guild and the Banners to boycott the Institute for Youth Fitness. 
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r -= 1; staal_marcher_support -= 2; labor_dissent += 10; knight_dissent += 10

Our explicit rejection of the Banners participation in the program has caused discontent within both the Greater Worker's Guild and the Banners, who have nonetheless reluctantly yielded to the party leadership’s decision. 

As a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> party, we cannot lend our support to what is, in essence, a thinly veiled rearmament scheme.